# Context

## Why This Way
Observation had to be read-only so a coding agent can watch a run
without draining it or changing task status. `inspect` therefore
opens the store with OpenStoreReadonly, and stopping an event
observer only stops the observer.

## Gotchas
- Worker log views resolve paths only from the published attempt
  (LogDir and fixed patterns), never from a path the viewer
  supplies. This keeps the dashboard from reading arbitrary files.
- The stream-json output switch applies to new Claude attempts.
  Existing runs keep their old executable and output mode until
  restarted normally.
- Event `data` is absent on older records; consumers must treat it
  as optional. `progress: "unknown"` means output alone proves
  nothing, not that the worker failed.

